This package is a port of the `server` package from pi
(https://github.com/earendil-works/pi), pinned at commit
8eb2bccf2603c28907ef3a583a04cafb1af284ae.

Provenance: this is a fork-and-adapt port, not a clean-room reimplementation.
The upstream sources were read directly and their structure, naming and
algorithms were carried across; the changes are the adaptations to this
repository's runtime and module layout, summarized below.

The execution plan for this milestone pins `d6af72e`. That commit exists and is
an ancestor of the tree above, but it is not the tree these files were copied
from, so the pin recorded here is the one that describes the actual source. A
provenance line naming a commit nobody read is worse than a stale one.

Adaptations, in order of how widely they apply:

  1. Every file: relative specifiers no longer carry a `.ts` suffix, as this
     repository's `check-ts-relative-imports` invariant requires.
  2. Class privacy: 86 `private` members across five files became ES `#private`
     fields, with their `this.<name>` references rewritten to `this.#<name>`.
     The public `get closed()` on `UnixByteConnection` is deliberately left
     public: it is a required member of the `ByteConnection` interface.
  3. Promise constructors: eight of the nine `new Promise` sites became
     `Promise.withResolvers()`. `ProtocolTestClient.nextFrom()` keeps its
     constructor and says why in a comment — it resolves a value derived from a
     predicate by the waiter loop in `receive()`, which a deferred cannot
     express.
  4. Node builtins: named imports from `node:crypto`, `node:fs/promises`,
     `node:net`, `node:path`, `node:events` became namespace imports with
     qualified call sites. Three functions took a parameter named `path`, which
     the module import then shadowed; those parameters are renamed.
  5. Types shared with packages this repository does not have:
     `Context`, `BACKGROUND_CONTEXT`, `TODO_CONTEXT` and `withAbortSignal` come
     from `@oh-my-pi/chord/context` instead of `pi-agent-core`, which is a pure
     re-export upstream. `SessionMetadata` is declared in `src/types.ts` with
     all six upstream fields verbatim, including `legacyParentSessionPath`,
     which nothing here reads. `MaybePromise` is re-exported from
     `@oh-my-pi/pi-utils/acp/protocol` so it has one owner.
  6. `NodeJS.Timeout` became `Timer` by this repository's convention. This is
     not a typecheck requirement: `NodeJS.Timeout` compiles here too.
  7. Tests: the runner moved from `vitest` to `bun:test`, which `bun:test` has
     no `vi.waitFor` for; `test/helpers.ts` supplies one polling helper in its
     place. Two conformance cases were additionally rewritten because Bun
     1.3.14's `expect(p).rejects` does not settle when the rejection arrives
     after the expectation was created. Both cases assert the same contract as
     upstream — see bead `epic-j0yo` for the minimal reproduction.

Every `src/` file differs from its upstream counterpart, so none is listed as
copied verbatim. The `#private` conversion alone touches all seventeen.

Added by this port, with no upstream counterpart: `LICENSE`, `NOTICE`,
`CHANGELOG.md`, `tsconfig.json` and `package.json` were rewritten for this
repository, and `test/helpers.ts` plus `src/testing/memory-session-repo.ts`
are new. Upstream's `vitest.config.ts`, `tsconfig.build.json` and
`tsconfig.test.json` were dropped — the runner change removes the first, and
AGENTS.md forbids the `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json` build the other two served.

The `package.json` `exports` map also gained explicit `./testing` and `./unix`
entries. The wildcard `./*` entry maps `./unix` to `./src/unix.ts`, which does
not exist, so both documented subpaths were unreachable until they were named.

